definition:
    What happens when an unstable nucleus changes into a steadier one and gives off radiation. It happens by itself, and heating a material or changing it chemically hardly affects it. Radioactivity is natural: it is found in rocks, in the air, in food, in space and in your own body. Henri Becquerel discovered it in 1896 in a uranium mineral.

debunking_snippet:
    “Radioactivity is something humans created.” It is as old as the Earth. People only learned to find it, measure it and use it.
